{"toolCallId":"call_9edf5279b92d4d419f42ae1d962ecbfd","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"53:| `PLACEHOLDER_FILLED` | ERROR or WARNING | Core files | No unfilled template tokens. A v2.3 doc warns while Draft |\n54-| `LEVEL_DECLARED`     | INFO     | spec.md       | Level explicitly stated in metadata            |\n55-| `AC_COVERAGE`        | INFO     | acceptance-criteria.md | Advisory traceability scan over each criterion's Verification cell (on by default; `SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE_ENFORCE=true` makes an under-floor result fail) |\n56-| `AC_CLOSURE`         | ERROR    | acceptance-criteria.md | Closure gate for Levels 2/3/3+: unmet criteria block a completion claim, waivers must cite a real ADR |\n57-| `CONTINUITY_FRESHNESS` | WARNING | completion claims | Opt-in strict-only completion freshness check |\n58-| `ANCHORS_VALID`      | ERROR    | spec docs with anchored templates | Anchors present, paired and not nested (adr-NNN may hold adr-NNN-*); a v2.3 doc also keeps each anchor its template requires |\n59-| `FOLDER_NAMING`      | ERROR    | Folder path   | Folder follows ###-short-name convention       |\n60-| `FRONTMATTER_VALID`  | ERROR    | spec docs     | YAML frontmatter properly structured           |\n61-| `COMPLEXITY_MATCH`   | WARNING  | All levels    | Content metrics match declared level           |\n62-| `AI_PROTOCOLS`       | ERROR    | Level 3/3+    | AI execution protocols present                 |\n63-| `LEVEL_MATCH`        | ERROR    | All files     | Level consistent across all spec files         |\n64-| `SPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY` | ERROR  | spec docs, goal.md | Anchor sufficiency; for `goal.md` also the durable budget (one limit: fail past 4000) and binding-row existence |\n65-| `FRONTMATTER_VALUES` | WARNING  | packet docs   | `contextType` or `importance_tier` outside sk-create-frontmatter's `frontmatter-values.json`; aliases are legal |\n66-| `SOURCE_TAGS`        | WARNING  | research/ + review/ | `[SOURCE: path:line]` tags that name a gone file, a moved file or a line past the end, in packets created after the cutoff |\n67-\n68-> **Partial reference:** The table above covers the most commonly-encountered rules. The authoritative, complete rule set and their canonical severities live in [`runtime/cli/lib/validator-registry.json`](../../runtime/cli/lib/validator-registry.json).\n69-\n70-### AC_CLOSURE\n71-\n72-`AC_CLOSURE` decides whether a packet may be closed. It is registered at ERROR severity and runs by default; set `SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE=false` to opt out.\n73-\n74-**Rule ID:** `AC_CLOSURE`\n75-\n76-**Scope:** Levels 2, 3 and 3+. Level 1 keeps acceptance criteria inline in `spec.md` and is never gated.\n77-\n78-**Rollout:** forward-only behind `SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE_CUTOFF` (default `2026-08-30`), compared against the `Created` date in the packet's `spec.md` metadata table. A packet created on or before the cutoff, or whose date cannot be read, is advisory on **every** branch — presence, waiver integrity and completion alike — and is never blocked. A malformed override falls back to the default rather than being compared as a string, which would otherwise grandfather the whole repository. This mirrors the `CANONICAL_SAVE_CUTOFF` pattern rather than introducing a third grandfathering mechanism.\n79-\n80-**Failure modes:**\n81-\n82-| Condition | Result |\n83-|---|---|\n84-| Post-cutoff packet with no `acceptance-criteria.md` | `fail` — the document is required at these levels |\n85-| A row marked `Waived` or `Superseded` naming no ADR | `fail` — an unbacked waiver is not a pass |\n86-| A criterion row that cannot be parsed, or an unbalanced code fence | `fail` — a dropped row would empty the table and close the packet |\n87-| Duplicate criterion ids | `fail` — the tally is ambiguous |\n88-| A row citing an ADR that `decision-record.md` does not contain | `fail` — the record is the whole justification |\n89-| A packet claiming completion with an `Unmet` row | `fail` — this is the closure gate |\n90-| An `Unmet` row while the packet is still in progress | `info` — work in progress is expected to carry open criteria |\n91-| Pre-cutoff packet | `info` — grandfathered |\n92-\n93-**Waiver contract:** a criterion may only be dropped or replaced through a decision record. The Waiver cell must name `ADR-NNN`, and every ADR it names must be declared in `decision-record.md` as a heading, a bold list item or a table row, outside any code fence. `ADR-1` and `ADR-001` are the same record.\n--\n267:## 4. PLACEHOLDER_FILLED\n268-\n269-**Severity:** ERROR, or WARNING for an unfilled token in a doc stamped v2.3 or later while its status is Draft  \n270-**Description:** Detects unfilled template placeholders that should be replaced with actual content.\n271-\n272-### Patterns Detected\n273-\n274-| Pattern                                              | Status  | Action Required           |\n275-| ---------------------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------- |\n276-| `[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: ...]`                             | FLAGGED | Replace with actual value |\n277-| `[NEEDS_CLARIFICATION: ...]` / `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION: ...]` | FLAGGED | Resolve and replace |\n278-| `[OPTIONAL: ...]`                                    | IGNORED | Optional content          |\n279-\n280-### Files Scanned\n281-\n282-- `spec.md`\n283-- `plan.md`\n284-- `tasks.md`\n285-- `acceptance-criteria.md` (if exists)\n286-- `decision-record.md` (if exists)\n287-\n288-### Lifecycle For Docs Stamped v2.3 Or Later\n289-\n290-A doc whose `SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE` stamp names version v2.3 or later ships every authoring hint as a `[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: ...]` token. For such a doc the rule reads the Status of `spec.md` and decides the severity of each unfilled token. A v2.3 `spec.md` has every table row whose first cell is Status read, anywhere in the file and including one inside a fenced code block, and a row that reads as complete wins over the first row; an older `spec.md` is read by its first such row.\n291-\n292-| Status in `spec.md` | Unfilled `[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: ...]` token | `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION: ...]` |\n293-| ------------------- | --------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n294-| Draft               | WARNING                                 | ERROR                        |\n295-| Any other value     | ERROR                                   | ERROR                        |\n296-\n297-A doc with an older stamp, or none, keeps the ERROR it always had, and Draft changes nothing for it. The orchestrator reads every authored doc that is present. The shell mirror reads `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `decision-record.md`, and it adds `acceptance-criteria.md`, `implementation-summary.md` and `goal.md` only when they carry the stamp. A warning never fails `--strict`. The status word must be exactly Draft, so Planned, In Progress and Complete all count as any other value.\n298-\n299-### Excluded Paths\n300-\n301-- `**/scratch/**` - Scratch files are never scanned\n302-- `**/memory/**` - Generated continuity artifacts use different validation (ANCHORS_VALID)\n303-- `**/templates/**` - Template files are expected to have placeholders\n304-\n305-### Examples\n306-\n307-❌ **Fail:**\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w27ef8e22cd/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"ac0891","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
