{"toolCallId":"call_f01815dad50844e6aad76ae9fdac2f6b","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"Output from command in shell 8e5aeb:\n\nSpec Folder Validation v3.0.0\n\n  Folder: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w27ef8e22cd/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\n  Level:  3\n  Engine: orchestrator\n\n+ FILE_EXISTS: All required files present for Level 3\n! PLACEHOLDER_FILLED: 104 unfilled value token(s) in a Draft packet. Fill each one before the status leaves Draft\n    - spec.md:3: description: \"[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What is broken, missing, or inefficient? 2-3 sentences describing the specific pain poin\n    - spec.md:23: **Key Decisions**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Major decision 1], [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Major decision 2]\n    - spec.md:25: **Critical Dependencies**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Blocking dependency]\n    - spec.md:35: | **Priority** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: P0/P1/P2] |\n    - spec.md:48: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What is broken, missing, or inefficient? 2-3 sentences describing the specific pain point.]\n    - spec.md:51: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: One-sentence outcome statement. What does success look like?]\n    - spec.md:61: - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Deliverable 1]\n    - spec.md:62: - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Deliverable 2]\n    - spec.md:63: - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Deliverable 3]\n    - spec.md:66: - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Excluded item 1] - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: why]\n    - spec.md:67: - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Excluded item 2] - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: why]\n    - spec.md:73: | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: path/to/file.js] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Modify/Create/Delete] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Brief description] |\n    - spec.md:86: | REQ-001 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Requirement description] |\n    - spec.md:92: | REQ-002 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Requirement description] |\n    - spec.md:104: - **SC-001**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Primary measurable outcome]\n    - spec.md:105: - **SC-002**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Secondary measurable outcome]\n    - spec.md:116: | Dependency | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: System/API] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What if blocked] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Fallback plan] |\n    - spec.md:117: | Risk | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Risk description] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: High/Med/Low] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Mitigation strategy] \n    - spec.md:127: - **NFR-P01**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Response time target - e.g., <200ms p95]\n    - spec.md:130: - **NFR-S01**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Auth requirement - e.g., JWT tokens required]\n    - spec.md:133: - **NFR-R01**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Uptime target - e.g., 99.9%]\n    - spec.md:141: - Empty input: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: How system handles]\n    - spec.md:142: - Maximum length: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Limit and behavior]\n    - spec.md:145: - External service failure: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Fallback behavior]\n    - spec.md:146: - Network timeout: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Retry strategy]\n    - spec.md:149: - Partial completion: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Recovery behavior]\n    - spec.md:150: - Session expiry: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: User experience]\n    - spec.md:159: | Scope | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: /25] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Files: X, LOC: Y, Systems: Z] |\n    - spec.md:160: | Risk | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: /25] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Auth: Y/N, API: Y/N, Breaking: Y/N] |\n    - spec.md:161: | Research | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: /20] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Investigation needs] |\n    - spec.md:162: | Multi-Agent | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: /15] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Workstreams: X] |\n    - spec.md:163: | Coordination | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: /15] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Dependencies: X] |\n    - spec.md:164: | **Total** | **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: /100]** | **Level 3** |\n    - spec.md:173: | R-001 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Risk] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: H/M/L] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: H/M/L] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Strategy] |\n    - spec.md:180: ### US-001: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Title] (Priority: P0)\n    - spec.md:182: **As a** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: user type], **I want** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: needed behavior], **so that** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: bene\n    - spec.md:188: ### US-002: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Title] (Priority: P1)\n    - spec.md:190: **As a** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: user type], **I want** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: needed behavior], **so that** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: bene\n    - spec.md:200: - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Question 1 requiring clarification]\n    - spec.md:201: - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Question 2 requiring clarification]\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w27ef8e22cd/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"ada680","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_f11e0070e1cb45549dca6ca1cd0a8d3a","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"### Lifecycle For Docs Stamped v2.3 Or Later\n\nA doc whose `SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE` stamp names version v2.3 or later ships every authoring hint as a `[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: ...]` token. For such a doc the rule reads the Status of `spec.md` and decides the severity of each unfilled token. A v2.3 `spec.md` has every table row whose first cell is Status read, anywhere in the file and including one inside a fenced code block, and a row that reads as complete wins over the first row; an older `spec.md` is read by its first such row.\n\n| Status in `spec.md` | Unfilled `[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: ...]` token | `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION: ...]` |\n| ------------------- | --------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| Draft               | WARNING                                 | ERROR                        |\n| Any other value     | ERROR                                   | ERROR                        |\n\nA doc with an older stamp, or none, keeps the ERROR it always had, and Draft changes nothing for it. The orchestrator reads every authored doc that is present. The shell mirror reads `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `decision-record.md`, and it adds `acceptance-criteria.md`, `implementation-summary.md` and `goal.md` only when they carry the stamp. A warning never fails `--strict`. The status word must be exactly Draft, so Planned, In Progress and Complete all count as any other value.\n\n### Excluded Paths\n\n- `**/scratch/**` - Scratch files are never scanned\n- `**/memory/**` - Generated continuity artifacts use different validation (ANCHORS_VALID)\n- `**/templates/**` - Template files are expected to have placeholders\n\n### Examples\n\n❌ **Fail:**\n```markdown\n## Metadata\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Type** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Feature type] |  ← FLAGGED\n```\n\n✅ **Pass:**\n```markdown\n## Metadata\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Type** | Feature |\n```\n\n### How to Fix\n\nReplace placeholder text with actual content:\n\n1. Find the flagged line in the output\n2. Replace `[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: description]` with the actual value\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w27ef8e22cd/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"f70b98","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
